settings-entry-description-normalize-chart-volume = Evens out volume differences between songs. Applies to charts and song previews.
settings-entry-description-normalize-system-bgm-volume = Evens out volume differences between BGMs on the song select, decide, and result screens.
settings-entry-description-master-volume = The overall volume of BMZ Player.
settings-entry-description-key-volume = The volume of sounds played when you press keys (keysounds).
settings-entry-description-bgm-volume = The volume of the backing track that plays automatically during play.
settings-entry-description-preview-volume = The volume of song previews on the song select screen.
settings-entry-description-system-bgm-volume = The volume of the BGM on the song select, decide, and result screens.
settings-entry-description-system-se-volume = The volume of sound effects for menus and screen changes.
settings-entry-description-input-offset = Shifts when key presses are judged, relative to the sound. Use it to correct input device delay. If you get many SLOW, adjust toward +.
settings-entry-description-visual-offset = Shifts when notes appear to reach the judgement line, relative to the sound. If you get many FAST, adjust toward -. If you get many SLOW, adjust toward +.
settings-entry-description-visual-offset-auto-adjust = Gradually adjusts the visual offset to match your timing during play. Turn it off once the timing feels right.
settings-entry-description-judge-algorithm = Decides which note is judged when notes are close together in the same lane. If unsure, keep COMBO.
settings-entry-description-fast-slow-display-scope = How FAST / SLOW is shown. With the threshold mode, it is also shown on PGREAT when the timing is off by at least the set number of ms.
settings-entry-description-fast-slow-display-threshold = In threshold mode, how far off a PGREAT must be to show FAST / SLOW. Set it to 0 to show it for every judgement.
settings-entry-description-rule-mode = Switches the timing windows, gauges, and score calculation together. Scores are saved separately for each rule.
settings-entry-description-ln-mode-policy = Chooses whether long notes are played as LN, CN, or HCN. AUTO follows the chart when it specifies a type. FORCE always uses your choice.
settings-entry-description-gauge = Changes how the gauge rises and drops, and what counts as a clear. NORMAL is a good start, and EASY helps with hard songs.
settings-entry-description-gauge-auto-shift = Chooses whether to keep playing on another gauge when you fail. BEST CLEAR records the highest gauge you cleared.
settings-entry-description-bottom-shiftable-gauge = The lowest gauge that gauge auto shift can record.
settings-entry-description-random = Changes which lanes the notes fall in. RANDOM shuffles whole lanes, and S-RANDOM moves each note separately.
settings-entry-description-double-option = Changes the layout when playing with both sides. FLIP swaps the 1P and 2P sides, and BATTLE gives both sides the same chart to play against each other.
settings-entry-description-hs-fix = When the BPM changes during a song, chooses which BPM sets the note speed.
settings-entry-description-target = The score you compare against during play, such as a rank goal like AAA or a top IR score.
settings-entry-description-assist = Features that help you play, such as wider timing windows. Except for display-only features, an assist that takes effect records clears as ASSIST and does not save scores.
settings-entry-description-bga-mode = Chooses whether to show background videos and images (BGA) during play. AUTO shows them only in autoplay and replays.
settings-entry-description-bga-expand = How BGA is scaled to fit its area. KEEP ASPECT keeps the original proportions.
settings-entry-description-auto-play = Plays the notes automatically. Scores are not saved.
settings-entry-description-session-mode = Chooses how to play: normal, practice for a section, autoplay, or a battle.
settings-entry-description-key-mode-conversion = Plays a chart converted to another key mode (DP, 9K, or 6K). Scores from converted plays are not saved.
settings-entry-description-seven-to-nine-pattern = When converting 7-key charts to 9 buttons, chooses which buttons the turntable and keys are assigned to.
settings-entry-description-seven-to-nine-type = When converting 7-key charts to 9 buttons, chooses how turntable notes are handled.
settings-entry-description-seven-to-nine-rule-mode = For 7-key charts converted to 9 buttons, chooses whether to use 7-key or 9-button timing and gauges.
settings-entry-description-play-exit-hold = How long to hold E1 and E2 to quit during play.
settings-entry-description-assist-expand-judge = Widens or narrows the timing windows using the judge window settings below.
settings-entry-description-assist-judge-area = Shows the range where notes can be judged on the lanes.
settings-entry-description-assist-mark-note = Marks notes that were added by conversion or assists.
settings-entry-description-assist-bpm-guide = Shows where the BPM changes on the lanes.
settings-entry-description-assist-scroll-mode = Chooses whether to remove or add changes in note scroll speed (SCROLL).
settings-entry-description-assist-long-note-mode = Removes long notes, or adds long notes of the selected type.
settings-entry-description-assist-mine-mode = Removes mines, or adds them at the selected kind of position.
settings-entry-description-assist-auto-scratch = Plays the scratch lane automatically. Only a clear is saved, as ASSIST EASY.
settings-entry-description-assist-scroll-section = When adding SCROLL changes, sets how many sections the chart is split into.
settings-entry-description-assist-scroll-rate = The chance of adding a SCROLL change to each section.
settings-entry-description-assist-long-note-rate = The chance of turning a note into a long note.
settings-entry-description-assist-extra-note-depth = When adding notes, sets how many nearby notes are used as a reference.
settings-entry-description-assist-extra-note-scratch = Also adds notes to the turntable when adding notes.
settings-entry-description-assist-extra-note-type = Kept for compatibility with beatoraja settings. Changing it currently has no effect.
settings-entry-description-assist-key-judge-rate = The key timing windows as a percentage of normal. 100% is normal.
settings-entry-description-assist-scratch-judge-rate = The turntable timing windows as a percentage of normal. 100% is normal.
settings-entry-description-assist-long-note-margin-rate = The timing margin for releasing long notes as a percentage of normal. 100% is normal.
settings-entry-description-misslayer-duration = How long the image shown on a miss (miss layer) stays on screen.
settings-entry-description-note-retention = Keeps normal notes at the judgement line until they are judged.
settings-entry-description-show-ln-tail-cap = Shows a dedicated image at the end of long notes.
settings-entry-description-guide-se = Plays a guide sound at the right timing for each judgement.
settings-entry-description-hispeed = The hi-speed multiplier used in CLASSIC. Larger values make notes fall faster.
settings-entry-description-hispeed-mode = How hi-speed is set. FLOATING uses a green number and sets the speed for each song's BPM automatically. With HS-FIX, LR2 treats the hi-speed as the multiplier at BPM 150.
settings-entry-description-normal-hispeed-level = The speed level used in NORMAL. Each level from 1 to 20 has a fixed green number.
settings-entry-description-classic-hispeed-step = How much one hi-speed change adds or removes in CLASSIC.
settings-entry-description-floating-hispeed-step = How much one hi-speed change adds or removes in FLOATING.
settings-entry-description-sudden-enabled = Enables the cover that hides the top of the lane (SUDDEN+).
settings-entry-description-sudden = How much of the top of the lane SUDDEN+ hides.
settings-entry-description-lift-enabled = Enables raising the judgement line (LIFT).
settings-entry-description-lift = How far LIFT raises the judgement line.
settings-entry-description-hispeed-auto-adjust = Adjusts hi-speed automatically so the green number stays the same when you move a lane cover or LIFT.
settings-entry-description-hidden-enabled = Enables the cover that hides the bottom of the lane (HIDDEN+).
settings-entry-description-hidden = How much of the area near the judgement line HIDDEN+ hides.
settings-entry-description-target-green-number = The green number kept in FLOATING. Smaller values look faster. 300 is about 0.5 seconds.
settings-entry-description-note-display-duration = How long notes stay visible when CONSTANT is on.
settings-entry-description-constant = Keeps the time notes are visible constant, even when the BPM or SCROLL changes.
settings-entry-description-constant-fade = How long notes fade at the edge of the visible range with CONSTANT.
settings-entry-description-select-input-mode = Chooses the key layout for controlling the song select screen: 7K/14K or 9K.
settings-entry-description-analog-scratch = Treats the controller turntable as analog, so input follows how far you spin it.
settings-entry-description-analog-scratch-sensitivity = How responsive the analog turntable is. Higher values react to smaller movements.
settings-entry-description-analog-scratch-threshold = How long after you stop spinning before the turntable counts as stopped.
settings-entry-description-analog-ticks-per-scroll = How far you spin the turntable to move one row on the song select screen.
settings-entry-description-lane-cover-step = How far one press of Up/Down moves SUDDEN+, HIDDEN+, or LIFT during play. 1000 is the whole lane. Holding E2 always moves it by 1.
settings-entry-description-lane-cover-hold-delay-ms = How long to hold Up/Down before SUDDEN+, HIDDEN+, or LIFT starts moving continuously.
settings-entry-description-lane-cover-hold-step = How far SUDDEN+, HIDDEN+, or LIFT moves every 1/60 second while Up/Down is held. 1000 is the whole lane.
settings-entry-description-lane-cover-wheel-step = How far one notch of the mouse wheel moves SUDDEN+, HIDDEN+, or LIFT during play. 1000 is the whole lane. Holding E2 moves it by 1 per notch.
settings-entry-description-keyboard-release-bounce = Prevents a key from being detected as pressed again right after you release it. 0 turns this off.
settings-entry-description-controller-release-bounce = Prevents a button from being detected as pressed again right after you release it. 0 turns this off.
settings-entry-description-hispeed-direction = Chooses whether this key raises or lowers hi-speed when pressed while holding E1.
settings-entry-description-difficulty-table-level-display = Chooses whether difficulty table folders show the table's level or the level written in the chart.
settings-entry-description-random-select = Shows an item in the song list that picks a song at random.
settings-entry-description-random-mix-target-level = The chart level a random course is centered on.
settings-entry-description-random-mix-max-level = The highest chart level included in a random course.
settings-entry-description-random-mix-min-level = The lowest chart level included in a random course.
settings-entry-description-random-mix-bpm-range = The allowed BPM difference between songs in a random course.
settings-entry-description-random-mix-max-bpm = The highest BPM included in a random course.
settings-entry-description-random-mix-min-bpm = The lowest BPM included in a random course.
settings-entry-description-random-mix-stages = The number of songs in a random course.
settings-entry-description-replay-auto-save = Saves a replay automatically when a play ends.
settings-entry-description-replay-compress = Compresses saved replays to make the files smaller.
settings-entry-description-replay-slot-rule = When a replay is saved to this slot automatically. With SCORE UPDATE, it is saved only when you beat your best score.
settings-entry-description-language = The language for menus and setting descriptions. Song titles and skin text do not change.
settings-entry-description-show-fps = Shows the number of frames drawn per second (FPS) on screen.
settings-entry-description-audio-backend = How sound is output. If unsure, keep Auto select. On Windows with an ASIO device, ASIO may reduce delay.
settings-entry-description-audio-output-mode = Shared low latency and Exclusive reduce sound delay. Exclusive silences other apps. Press Apply after changing it.
settings-entry-description-audio-sample-rate = The output sample rate. If unsure, keep the automatic setting.
settings-entry-description-audio-buffer-mode = Chooses whether the audio buffer size is automatic or fixed. Choose Fixed to reduce delay.
settings-entry-description-audio-buffer-size = Smaller values reduce sound delay, but too small makes the sound crackle. Choose the smallest value that plays cleanly.
settings-entry-description-audio-output-device = The device that plays sound. If yours is not listed, press Refresh device list.
settings-entry-description-audio-asio-driver = The ASIO driver to use. If yours is not listed, press Refresh device list.
settings-entry-description-audio-output-channel = On ASIO devices with many outputs, chooses which outputs play the sound.
settings-entry-description-video-window-mode = Chooses windowed or fullscreen display. Fullscreen may reduce display delay.
settings-entry-description-video-window-size = The window width and height. Takes effect the next time you start BMZ Player.
settings-entry-description-video-internal-resolution = Chooses whether to render at the window's resolution or the skin's resolution.
settings-entry-description-video-monitor = The monitor used for fullscreen. Takes effect the next time you start BMZ Player.
settings-entry-description-video-vsync = Chooses whether to prevent screen tearing. Preventing it adds a little display delay.
settings-entry-description-video-frame-latency = Low latency reduces display delay. Choose Stable if the picture stutters.
settings-entry-description-video-target-fps = The maximum number of frames drawn per second. 0 means no limit.
settings-entry-description-video-background-fps = The frame limit while another window is active. Lower values reduce load on your computer.
settings-entry-description-video-renderer = How the screen is rendered. If unsure, keep Auto select. Takes effect the next time you start BMZ Player.
settings-key-binding-description = Assigns the key or button used for this action.

